<Page title="Make it your own."><div data-handoff-page data-source="fixture">
  <a class="back-link" data-context-return href="/browse/">Keep browsing the catalog</a><h1>Make it your own.</h1>
  <p class="lead">Installing is optional. Stay with the catalog, visit the hosted store, or create a store for the library you already have.</p>
  <dl class="experience-list"><div><dt>Browse here</dt><dd>Quick title reading and watch options. No install or home server; this preview contains fictional sample records.</dd></div><div><dt>Visit the hosted 3D store</dt><dd>A stocked, walkable store with streaming link-outs. No media server or API key needed. Providers may require their own subscription or sign-in.</dd></div><div><dt>Run your own store</dt><dd>Choose your streaming services, or connect an existing Plex, Jellyfin or Emby library. A local install starts empty until you make those choices. There is no built-in folder scanner.</dd></div></dl>
  <h2>Your first successful visit</h2><ol class="first-success"><li>Try the hosted store first if you only want to browse. You do not need to install anything.</li><li>For your own store, open the maintained quick-start guide on the computer that will run it. Choose the Windows, macOS, Linux launcher or Docker instructions that fit you.</li><li>At the opening-day setup terminal, choose the streaming services you use. The bundled selection works without a key or a media server. Leaving every service off is a valid empty store.</li><li>If you already have Plex, Jellyfin or Emby, connect it inside your own installation. This public catalog never asks for those credentials or looks for devices on your network.</li><li>Browse a shelf and open a title. Streaming checkout opens a provider’s search or watch page; it is not successful playback. Personal-library playback depends on your server, access and supported media.</li></ol>
  <p><a class="button" data-cta="installation_guide_visit" href="https://github.com/halcyon-video/halcyon-video#quick-start" rel="external noreferrer">Open the installation guide</a></p>
  <p><a class="back-link" data-cta="installation_guide_visit" href="https://github.com/halcyon-video/halcyon-video/releases" rel="external noreferrer">View releases and release notes</a></p>
  <p class="muted">The guide is the maintained setup path, not a one-click installer. No fresh installation or physical-device acceptance is claimed by this preview. There is no paid tier introduced here.</p>
  <p><a class="back-link" data-store-bridge href="/store/">Explore the 3D store</a></p>
